{:id :EACL-FORMAL-034
 :status :fixed
 :discovered-by :differential
 :seed-or-trace
 "formal-cljs-smoke/then-counterexample-replay/same-persistent-nrepl"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :availability
 :affected-versions
 ["PR 101 commit 2c3065e2468c199ad9a2947766471936bd8e42c2"]
 :affected-backends [:shared]
 :root-cause
 "The CLJS formal smoke launcher called cljs.main/-main inside the persistent nREPL. The CLI lifecycle calls shutdown-agents, permanently terminating the executor used by Clojure future and making later concurrency regressions fail with RejectedExecutionException."
 :fix
 "The launcher now calls cljs.build.api/build, runs the Node suite, and asserts through the same nREPL that a future still completes. Formal evidence no longer depends on whether CLJS compilation ran before JVM concurrency tests."
 :closing-evidence
 ["formal/smoke/cljs/run runtime postcondition :eacl.formal/agent-executor-alive"
  "eacl.characterization-fixture-test/formal-cljs-smoke-preserves-persistent-nrepl-executors-test"
  "formal mutation :formal-cljs-smoke-terminates-agent-executors"]}
